s but his most popular  and  longest running role is playing sheriff  walt longmire  however the role of walt longmire almost  went to coach taylor or  more specifically the actor who played  him kyle chandler  chandler's turn as the coach on the nbc  show friday night lights brought him a  lot of industry buzz  he went on to other roles in many  acclaimed movies such as argo  zerodark 30 the wolf of wall street and  manchester by the sea  while chandler's early career included a  country movie the actor himself is a bit  of a joker and might have brought some  of the levity to the series that  longmire carries through the book series  as he's matured chandler has also  adopted a bit of the roguish tough  cowboy look that would have fit the  sheriff we all know  executive producer hunt baldwin grew up  in chicago and worked in advertising for  many years  his parents moved to wyoming and that  bold move inspired him to eventually  leave his safe existence  and move to los angeles to become a  full-time writer there he worked hard  for many years before eventually  fulfilling his dream  working with his writing partner john  covny on their series the closer  baldwin and company are both represented  by the same agent at talent agency caa  and it was that shared connection at caa  that gave rise to longmire  according to company they had talked to  their agent over the years about wanting  to do a modern western  company mentioned that he had been a big  fan of butch cassidy and the sundance  kid  their agent then mentioned that caa also  happened to be representing an author  named craig johnson who'd written a  series of modern day western centering  on a cowboy sheriff  according to company they read the cold  dish and said  about 10 pages in we knew it was  something we wanted to develop  baldwin and coveney's experience working  together on lapd police procedural the  closer was a big help when they began  developing longmire  they still needed an executive producer  with experience running a show though  luckily while at the closer they met and  worked closely with producer greer  shepard  so they set up a meeting with her to  discuss this new project  greer is a tv veteran she produced her  first series in 1997  nothing sacred one of her first big hits  as an executive producer was nip tuck in  2003  she was the perfect person to shepherd  two first-time creators through a  decidedly  unique police procedural according to  baldwin and companies interview with  assignment x  it took about three years from that  first sit down to longmire  eventually premiering on a e it quickly  became a relationship made in tv heaven  in fact  shepard mentioned in a 2012 interview  with the hollywood reporter that if she  could add  any writer to her staff she would quote  clone hunt baldwin and john coveny  there are many differences between craig  johnson's longmire books and  baldwin and shepard's longmire tv series  and while the book plots inspire the  storylines the series has created  many new stories in the books absaroka  county only had  5 murders in 24 years yet police  procedurals on tv tend to have  lots of murders because it makes for  very compelling television  in longmire there's a new murder almost  every episode  also in the books walt longmire's wife  isn't murdered but instead dies of  cancer  his wife's murder in the tv series is a  central plot point in the series but  one of the largest differences is  longmire himself  in the books walt longmire is witty many  would say he's riley humorous  in fact the books are often praised for  their humor but robert taylor plays  sheriff walt longmire straight  almost to a fault the only comedy we see  from tv walt longmire is when he makes  social or  technological faux pas a humor generated  from  everybody else's reactions to his  unwillingness to embrace the modern  world  in the few moments when walt says  something funny he doesn't  seem to realize it there are many  peculiarities that make longmire and its  protagonist  so memorable the fact walt doesn't have  a cell phone nor does he  ever use gloves the crime scenes are  just two but one of the most  well noted ticks is walt longmire's  devotion to rain your beer  rainier is a cheap beer that isn't found  all over comparable in price to pbr  and also owned by pabst brewing company  in an interview with the casper star  tribune  johnson explains he was surprised by how  long meyer has impacted rainier beer  johnson said i figured walt's not a  blueberry microbrew kind of guy  johnson also charges one very  inexpensive and unique item for speaking  at  any and all wyoming libraries a six-pack  of rainier  there is one more connection though the  longmire historic district in washington  is the location of mount rainier  national park  so perhaps that longmire rainier  connection may have influenced johnson  in naming his famous sheriff  there are no confirmed statements that  say walt's last name was inspired by his  favorite beer so  this might just be another mystery for  walt longmire but when it comes to tying  together supposed coincidences to suss  out the truth  there's nobody better check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

